From d2f887eb8c8ce6ba30a29a85a15e9c9ec15821f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:07:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v2): emit authenticated explorer frames and native input
 facts

Retain the exact 134-byte header and full transaction frames, native identities and input ordinals, coinbase/mint selectors, and checked payload/table byte ranges. Derive locations from native-decoded facts after byte-exact re-encoding against the authenticated body. Genesis retains its actual zero predecessor; only the existing CXX checkpoint adapter self-parents genesis. Historical input creation facts remain exclusively resolved by the durable DB owner.

Integration requires adding chronik_explorer.cpp wherever chronik_sync.cpp is compiled and registering test_chronik_explorer.cpp with the existing sync target dependencies. Rust CXX DTOs must add the contract WireRange, NativeWitness, NativeFullInput, NativeTx wire/lock/full_inputs, and NativeBlock header_wire[134]. No existing codec or Rust owner files changed.

Validation: isolated harness configured at /private/tmp/lotus-v2-explorer-producer-harness-20261015, focused native build -j2, chronik_explorer_test and existing chronik_sync_test pass. Tests cover exact header/frame/root/identity parity, coinbase presence, native mint/spend slots, all branch/path positions, chunk-crossing witnesses, canonical table offsets, maximum integers, malformed frames and profile bounds. This is native fixture/sync evidence, not CXX/Rust linked integration or node-startup evidence.
